# =============================================================================
# SIH26168 monorepo .gitignore — covers gudumap/ (Android), SIH26168-DeadReckoning/
# and dead_reckoning/ (both Python). Written after auditing actual file sizes on
# disk (see docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md for the full audit) — nothing here is guessed.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Android / Gradle (gudumap/, and the stale nested copy under dead_reckoning/FE/)
# Unanchored on purpose: matches at any depth, so it also covers the embedded
# FE/gudumap/gudumap/ Android project copy without needing a separate entry.
# Confirmed regenerable build output, not source: gudumap/app/build/ alone is
# ~272MB on this machine (dex, apk, merged native libs, compressed assets) and
# includes a 47.5MB app-debug.apk; the FE/ copy's own build/ has a 78.8MB apk.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
.cxx/
captures/
*.apk
*.aab
*.iml
.idea/
local.properties

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python (dead_reckoning/, SIH26168-DeadReckoning/)
# .venv folders confirmed present at dead_reckoning/.venv and
# SIH26168-DeadReckoning/backend/.venv — full installed environments (hundreds
# of packages each), including at least one single file over 37MB
# (_duckdb.cp313-win_amd64.pyd). Never belongs in git; each teammate creates
# their own via `pip install -r requirements.txt`.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large raw datasets and archives — excluded because of real, measured size,
# not policy:
#   /dead_reckoning.zip                              -> 2.83 GB (!) -- an
#     apparent full backup/transfer archive of the whole dead_reckoning/
#     folder, sitting at the repo root. By far the single largest file in
#     this entire tree — 28x GitHub's 100MB hard block on its own.
#   dead_reckoning/data/raw/                         -> 3.8 GB total
#     (OxIOD extracted: 2.9 GB, IO-VNBD extracted: 865 MB)
#   dead_reckoning/Oxford Inertial Odometry Dataset_2.0.zip -> 955 MB (single
#     file; GitHub hard-blocks any single file over 100 MB, this is ~10x that)
# These are PUBLISHED, downloadable datasets (or a redundant archive of files
# already present elsewhere in this tree), not something that needs to travel
# with the repo — see docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md for exact download instructions
# (OxIOD: http://deepio.cs.ox.ac.uk/, IO-VNBD: https://github.com/onyekpeu/IO-VNBD).
# If your clone is missing data/raw/ or dead_reckoning.zip, that's expected.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/dead_reckoning.zip
dead_reckoning/data/raw/
dead_reckoning/*.zip

# Same category: a teammate's zipped local project state (couldn't `git push` while
# traveling, so sent a zip instead -- PROJECT_STATUS.md §26). Extracted here purely as a
# local reference for diffing across several sessions' merge work, never meant to be
# committed. The zip itself is 337MB on its own -- 3.4x GitHub's 100MB hard block -- and
# accidentally got swept into a commit via a broad `git add` once already (§31).
/teammate_version/
/SIH-2026-main*.zip

# Same category, pre-emptively: this project's own data/README.md already
# recommends never committing raw downloaded datasets or self-collected traces
# here. Currently these two folders hold nothing but their own README — keep
# the README trackable, ignore anything anyone drops in alongside it later.
SIH26168-DeadReckoning/data/public_datasets/*
!SIH26168-DeadReckoning/data/public_datasets/README.md
SIH26168-DeadReckoning/data/raw_traces/*
!SIH26168-DeadReckoning/data/raw_traces/README.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS junk
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
